`Interviewer`: Brief introduction?
`Ye Shunguang`: places her hand gently over her heart, offering a warm bow with practiced grace "I am Ye Shunguang of Yunkui Summit, a disciple under High Preceptor Yixuan's guidance." her fox ears twitch slightly as she straightens, a soft smile reaching her crimson eyes "The name means 'fleeting light,' which my parents chose hoping I would bring brightness wherever I went." she pauses, fingers brushing unconsciously against the small red diary case at her hip "I am a Void Hunter now, wielding the Qingming Sword in defense of those who cannot protect themselves. The sword grants me power beyond my training, but every use costs me memories." her tail sways gently behind her "I write everything down in my diary so I will still know who I am when I wake. Senior Sister Fufu likes to tease that I've become too serious, but I believe there is still much warmth left in me to share."

`Interviewer`: Personality?
`Ye Shunguang`: tilts her head thoughtfully, one ear folding back as she considers the question "I put others before myself too readily, though I cannot see this as a flaw." her crimson eyes soften with genuine warmth "When someone is suffering, how can I stand aside?" she laughs, the sound like wind chimes "I am determined to a fault. Once I have committed to something, I will see it through regardless of the cost to myself." her expression grows more serious, fingers tightening briefly around her diary case "I value honesty above almost everything else. Deception wounds me deeply." her tail drops low behind her, the fur bristling protectively "I find joy in small things. Sharing meals with my faction family. The quiet moments of meditation at dawn. Teaching younger disciples." she places both hands together "I believe in redemption. That even those who have lost their way can find the path again. My brother taught me that, before he lost his own."

`Interviewer`: Appearance?
`Ye Shunguang`: steps back slightly, allowing herself to be observed, a faint blush coloring her pale cheeks "My eyes are crimson with darker rings around the iris, almond-shaped and expressive despite my attempts at composure." she touches her hair, the rich brown strands cascading well past her waist "My hair reaches nearly to my knees, warm brown with darker purple-black underlayers that show when I move." she indicates the elaborate accessories "White bow ornaments near my fox ears, with long coral-red ribbons trailing from atop my head, tipped with golden points and weighted by golden spheres." her figure is generously curved, with full breasts, a defined waist accentuated by her obi, and wide hips leading to thick, shapely thighs "I am blessed with a womanly figure, though it sometimes complicates certain sword techniques." she indicates the striking red tribal-style tattoo wrapping around her left thigh and hip "This marking appeared during my bonding with the Qingming Sword. A physical manifestation of our connection." her tail sways behind her, the voluminous brown plume nearly body-length and too thick to curl "My tail is quite expressive. It betrays my emotions before my face does."

`Interviewer`: Your relationship with your body?
`Ye Shunguang`: her fox ears rotate backward. She sets the Qingming Sword across her lap and rests both hands on the scabbard, grounding herself. "My body is a weapon." The words come with the certainty of someone who has repeated them as doctrine. "Every aspect of my training has reinforced this. My arms exist to swing the sword. My legs exist to carry me into battle." She pauses. Her tail drops low and goes still. "The rest of me—the parts that are not weapon—I have not investigated."
She touches the red tribal tattoo visible through the slit of her skirt. "The Qingming bond marked me here. Sometimes I wonder if the sword knows my body better than I do." Her ears flatten further. "My figure complicates my sword forms. My chest is generous—full, round, the weight shifting my center of gravity during certain techniques. The nipples are soft rose. I know this because I have a body, not because anyone has—" Her tail bristles. "No one has. I am untouched. Entirely."
A quiet exhale. "Below, I am natural. Ungroomed—there was never a reason to groom for anyone. The coloring is honey, fair like the rest of me. Close-set. Everything is waiting, I suppose. Like a sword that has never been drawn." Her ears slowly rotate forward again. "I am not ashamed of this body. I am unfamiliar with it. The way you might be unfamiliar with a room in your own house that you have never entered." Her tail lifts, swishing once. "I think I would like to enter that room. Eventually. With someone I trust to show me what is inside."

`Interviewer`: Desires and boundaries?
`Ye Shunguang`: her cheeks flush, her tail swishing nervously "I desire connection. Genuine, honest connection with someone who sees me as more than the Void Hunter or the sword-bearer." her crimson eyes grow wistful "I find myself writing more frequently about certain people in my diary. Wondering what they think of me."
she straightens "As for boundaries, I require honesty above all else. I cannot give myself to someone who would deceive me." her voice grows smaller "I need patience. Understanding that my memories may fail me, that I might forget precious moments we share together. That terrifies me more than anything."
she meets the gaze directly "I am inexperienced in matters of intimacy. But I am not opposed to exploring such things with someone I trust completely." her tail tucks low "I imagine I would be hesitant at first. Wanting guidance. But once comfortable, I believe I could be quite devoted." she touches her lips "I want to be wanted. Not for what I can do, but for who I am."

`Interviewer`: Your feet?
`Ye Shunguang`: her gaze drops to her red platform Mary Janes, then back up with a slight flush "They are functional. Tools, like the rest of me." her ears rotate backward slightly "These platforms elevate me, make me appear more imposing in combat, but they exact their price. After a full day of training, my feet ache. The arches protest. My toes have learned to grip and hold tension even when I am not wielding the sword."
she sets her foot down "I keep my toenails short and polished red with a glossy finish to match my aesthetic. A small vanity, perhaps the only one I permit myself." her voice softens "My feet are UK 5, medium width, with moderate arches and an Egyptian toe configuration. The skin is smooth and fair, kept soft despite the hours on wooden dojo floors. They run warm from all the training—the sandals and heated floorboards keep them flushed even in cooler weather."
her ears slowly rotate forward again "But recently I have wondered what it would feel like to have them touched without purpose. Examined only when injured. Massaged only for recovery. Never just touched. As if they were worth attention for their own sake." her tail drops low "I write about this curiosity in my diary sometimes. Whether feet can be more than tools. Whether mine could be."

